Braces inside a string literal in a code-block body neither open nor
close the literal: `"{"` does not swallow the rest of the file and `"}"`
does not end the block early; the statement after the literal still
formats (fmt.code_block_literals issue #255).
-- input.ssl --
:PROCEDURE Braces;
:DECLARE fnOpen, fnClose, aPair;
fnOpen := {|s|s+"{"};
fnClose := {|s|"}"+s};
aPair := {1,2};
:RETURN aPair;
:ENDPROC;
-- format --
:PROCEDURE Braces;
	:DECLARE fnOpen, fnClose, aPair;
	fnOpen := {|s| s + "{"};
	fnClose := {|s| "}" + s};
	aPair := {1, 2};
	:RETURN aPair;
:ENDPROC;
-- diagnostics --
-- diagnostics [--strict --info] --
